/*
  Localizable.strings (Spanish)
  Despacer

  Keys are the English source strings. SwiftUI literals (Text, Button, ...)
  and String(localized:) look them up in Bundle.main. %@ is a string argument.

  Do not translate: Despacer, Claude Code, Codex, Matt Senter, Senternet,
  Senternet LLC, other app names (CommandH, Weatherling, Burly, Comoji,
  Premail, Highwire, StockCar, Orgabot, Fix Siri, BeeReady, SeedMatrix),
  Slack, :emoji:, Cmd+H, "Hey Siri, do better.", or keyboard glyphs such as ⌘.
  Never use an em dash in a translation.

  When a string names a macOS feature or place, use Apple's official Spanish
  name for it: barra de menús, carpeta Aplicaciones, iniciar sesión,
  Ajustes del Sistema, Pegar desde otras apps, Permitir.

  Every key here must exist in every other .lproj, and every string the app
  shows must be a key here: scripts/check-localization.py enforces both.
*/


